    <string name="survive_title">🧭 Outdoor Orientation · Lost Survival</string>
    <string name="survive_sub">Sun / watch / Polaris / vegetation cues + the STOP rule · tap to expand</string>
    <string name="survive_1">☀️ Sun: rises east, sets west; at noon (northern hemisphere) it sits due south — the shortest shadow points north</string>
    <string name="survive_2">⌚ Watch: point the hour hand at the sun; the bisector of the angle to 12 o\'clock is due south (northern hemisphere)</string>
    <string name="survive_3">🌟 Night: extend the line of the Big Dipper\'s pointer stars about 5× to find Polaris — it marks true north</string>
    <string name="survive_4">🌲 Vegetation: the sunnier (south) side grows denser leaves and wider rings; moss favors the shaded bark</string>
    <string name="survive_5">⛰️ Lost: STOP first; recall the last known landmark; climb to a vantage and prefer retrace your route</string>
    <string name="survive_6">💧 People: follow streams downstream — villages and roads are more likely; stop moving at night, save battery and strength</string>
